{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm","id":1408575,"title":"Questions about something like \"Money-Shaman paradigm\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-16T13:59:51-07:00","id":1408575,"title":"Questions about something like \"Money-Shaman paradigm\"","content":"Hey guys! First of all, I am not a native english speaker, so sorry any mistakes in my post.<br /> <br /> So, i'm in a chronicle of MTA with others players, the game takes place New York city and all of us have characters with some urban integration and urban-kind paradigm. But, a players has this strange idea: He wants to create a money-based mage, probably a House Fortune one, but with a diferent kind of paradigm - the guy wants to be a &quot;money-shaman&quot;.<br /> <br /> Probably the dreamspeakers or euthanatos paradigms won't allow this kind of thing, this is the reason that he chooses the House Fortune.<br /> <br /> This is his idea: He want to be a mage who works with spirits (or elementals) of money/fortune/capitalism (the &quot;prime sphere&quot; will be capitalism [?]) and he wants to choose the own capitalism as a Totem. We advise he to take some God, like Hermes to be a totem, but he willing to take the own capitalism god-form as totem. He plans, in the future, to use both entropy and mind to have a &quot;good luck&quot; touch and manipulate everyone to provide resources to him. Yet, he too wants to have a &quot;money-spirit fetish&quot; in a coin that give a boost the fortune thing, making opportunities to earn more money by manipulating the surround area. And, of course, his have a idea for a future &quot;pot of greed&quot; talisman. His character wuold constantly seeks influence, power and control over city areas and influent people (like politicians, businessmen and bankers).<br /> <br /> I, particulary, have a lot of questions on it, but here have some of them:<br /> <br /> 1 - Is this possible?<br /> 2 - Won't the &quot;men in black&quot; track him fast and &quot;make everything&quot; disappear?<br /> 3 - I was thinking, the rotes in his paradigm may seens &quot;coincidental&quot;, but making money with the aid of magick and messing with the capitalist system won't be a higher chance to &quot;attract&quot; more paradox attention?<br /> 4 - Won't the Urban Spirit of the city be mad with someone messing up the natural flow of wealth of the city? I mean, this kind of spirit as an enemy can destroy his pretensions really fast...<br /> 5 - Let's assume that &quot;money elementals&quot; or &quot;spirit of capitalism&quot; does exist: what are the conditions for dealing with them? Them powers, charms, attributes, shape and limits? Will them have something like &quot;entropy 2&quot; thing? The more powerful ones can do the &quot;meme thing&quot; with &quot;entropy 5&quot;? Seems very hard to me.<br /> 6 - Is it even possible to have the Capitalism as a Totem???<br /> 7 - And a completely random question: if money elementals or fortune spirits does exist, is possible to cause financial loss to someone in a shaman way - causing harm or death of some sort of money spirit accompanying wealth of this guy? <br /> <br /> Any tips, answers and ideias about this would be great!<br /> <br /> Thank you all!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26367-wickedone","name":"WickedOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:21:06-07:00","id":1408577,"title":"","content":"Check out the revised Glasswalker tribebook, they have a totem in there called O' Mighty Dollar. It would probably be better for your pc to be a dreamspeaker the an order of Hermes if you want to go the shaman route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:45:44-07:00","id":1408581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408577#post1408577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out the revised Glasswalker tribebook, they have a totem in there called O' Mighty Dollar. It would probably be better for your pc to be a dreamspeaker the an order of Hermes if you want to go the shaman route.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I had completely forgotten about this totem and &quot;Easy Credit&quot;. But, won't O' Mighty Dolla' be stumbling block if PC want's to leave US? <br /> <br /> I agree that dreamspeaker tradition is better to a shaman, but I was reading the dreamspeark tradition book and &quot;the spirit ways&quot; and this kind of paradigm seens a bit contraditory with their way and it's hard to conciliate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user