ank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T14:46:35-07:00","id":1408583,"title":"","content":"Capitalism might be too abstract as a totem. He does have many smaller options though: The Dollar. Credit. The Invisible Hand. Luck. These are all totems currently available in werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:01:07-07:00","id":1408604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WickedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408582#post1408582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I had completely forgotten about this totem and &amp;quot;Easy Credit&amp;quot;. But, won't O' Mighty Dolla' be stumbling block if PC want's to leave US? <br /> <br /> I agree that dreamspeaker tradition is better to a shaman, but I was reading the dreamspeark tradition book and &amp;quot;the spirit ways&amp;quot; and this kind of paradigm seens a bit contraditory with their way and it's hard to conciliate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well being a shaman in the order of Hermes dosen't fit their paradigm either sooooo..........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:04:17-07:00","id":1408606,"title":"","content":"So a Syndicate Shaman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:10:45-07:00","id":1408608,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408583#post1408583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Capitalism might be too abstract as a totem. He does have many smaller options though: The Dollar. Credit. The Invisible Hand. Luck. These are all totems currently available in werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not too familiar with WTA, however these are the arguments that PC use to not choose Easy Credit or Invisible Hand: The Easy Credit's clients may not use coins or paper money, and he wants to use all forms of money, including the fetish thing and Invisible Hand &quot;repudiate any child who cheats or reneges on a bargain&quot; and he wants to cheat sometimes and have freedom to reneges a bargain.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm talking with him about the O' Mighty Dolla', but he's italian immigrant, the totem seens to be very territorialist. Lady Luck is very good, he wants something focused in money, maybe there's a solution here.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">However, I still with a lot of doubts about the &quot;money/wealth spirit/elemental&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408604#post1408604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well being a shaman in the order of Hermes dosen't fit their paradigm either sooooo..........</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Exactly! that's the problem! And what a problem...</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408606#post1408606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Syndicate Shaman?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A kind of... nevertheless he is on the side of &quot;traditions&quot;.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, I didn't want to forbid him to create such a character, but I don't see perspective or how this can works... A character like that it seems like an impossibility</span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26367-wickedone","name":"WickedOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:31:08-07:00","id":1408610,"title":"","content":"There has to be a good capitalist Totem what about Mammon? He is like capitalism personified, and we all know that every capitalist worships him /s/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T16:34:36-07:00","id":1408611,"title":"","content":"The american dream is to make a fortune and own things, being an immigrant to America the totem would pick him up in a heart beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T19:30:41-07:00","id":1408632,"title":"","content":"He'll be a Dreamspeaker and choose Mammom as Totem based on O' Mighty Dolla'... Now, I need to solve every other questions about money spirits etc. Any tips?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26367-wickedone","name":"WickedOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T19:34:29-07:00","id":1408634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408577#post1408577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out the revised Glasswalker tribebook, they have a totem in there called O' Mighty Dollar. It would probably be better for your pc to be a dreamspeaker the an order of Hermes if you want to go the shaman route.</div> </div> </div> </div>That IS what the book says. And then they give us totems that even Technocrats can take. Honestly, I think it is just up to the Mage, the Spirit, and compatibility and desire on both sides. If you have a good idea for a Hermetic with a Totem, then you should go for it. When they told us that even the most fanatical of MIB's could have totems even if they didn't realize it, all of the old rules went out the window.<br /> <br /> I think Fire Drake from the revised Get of Fenris book would make a decent Totem for a member of House Verditus, and Xaos/Thig could probably find common ground with Cockroach, Donna Matrix, and other Tech Totems. It should just be somewhat less common for Hermetics, who already start out on the right foot with Hermes from the Infinite Tapestry, and the fact that for many of the Hermetics, Totems and the humility that goes with them isn't really their schtick. Then again, they DO desire to be like Hermes the Thrice Great, who is described in Rev OoH as being &quot;the greatest of kings, the greatest of philosophers, and the greatest of priests.&quot; Undoubtedly, some in the Order will decide to go for it. And even though gods like Ra, Marduk, Hermes, Ishtar, Vulcan, and Odin will see more Hermetics looking to strike an alliance with them than the spirits that the Fera serve, money is always a draw and someone in charge of their Cabal's/Chantry's finances could easily seek out an alliance with whatever spirit embodies the concept of profit and wealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-16-2020, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T20:32:15-07:00","id":1408646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WickedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408608#post1408608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [COLOR=#000000][FONT=&amp;quot][SIZE=12px]<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not too familiar with WTA, however these are the arguments that PC use to not choose Easy Credit or Invisible Hand: The Easy Credit's clients may not use coins or paper money, and he wants to use all forms of money, including the fetish thing and Invisible Hand &quot;repudiate any child who cheats or reneges on a bargain&quot; and he wants to cheat sometimes and have freedom to reneges a bargain.</span></span></span><br /> ]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Totems have costs. You limit your freedom and thus ritually gain power from it. If he wants a totem that;s not going to limit him. Coyote is right there and more than wiling to &quot;help&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T21:25:28-07:00","id":1408651,"title":"","content":"I tried writing a response to this earlier on my phone, but kept getting pull away by RL and then it got lost when my phone logged me out &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> I think how well the idea can work depends a fair bit on how one chooses to interpret the word &quot;shaman,&quot; but I think there are at least two ways to handle this character concept:<br /> <br /> When saying they want to be a &quot;shaman,&quot; your player might simply mean &quot;a Mage whose magic is centred around summoning, interacting with, or binding spirits.&quot; If that is all, then a member of the Hermetic House Fortunae might actually work really well. As posts above have mentioned, the concept of &quot;capitalism&quot; is a bit abstract for the Middle Umbra. However, it seems rather appropriate for an entity of the High Umbra, and summoning Angels from the High Umbra has been a component of the Hermetic tradition for a long time now.<br /> <br /> The more specific connotation of the word &quot;shaman&quot; goes beyond just summoning and interacting with spirits, however. It also tends to include reverence for the larger system, not simply a desire to exploit it for your advantage, along with a role as a mediator between the community and the spirit-world. If that is the sort of thing you're looking for, an &quot;Urban Shaman&quot; Dreamspeaker inspired by the Glass Walker material cited above would likely be more appropriate. &quot;Pure&quot; capitalism is a bit at odds with the idea of a shamanistic character in this sense, but someone who played the role of &quot;mediator&quot; between people and &quot;the market&quot; might try to achieve &quot;balance&quot; through things like regulation, non-profit work, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T21:29:41-07:00","id":1408652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408646#post1408646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Totems have costs. You limit your freedom and thus ritually gain power from it. If he wants a totem that;s not going to limit him. Coyote is right there and more than wiling to &quot;help&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Coyote 2020, Make Dreamspeakers Great Again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T09:13:52-07:00","id":1408730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408652#post1408652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coyote 2020, Make Dreamspeakers Great Again!</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what those Coyote demand as a totem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T09:25:26-07:00","id":1408732,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408634#post1408634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That IS what the book says. And then they give us totems that even Technocrats can take. Honestly, I think it is just up to the Mage, the Spirit, and compatibility and desire on both sides. If you have a good idea for a Hermetic with a Totem, then you should go for it. When they told us that even the most fanatical of MIB's could have totems even if they didn't realize it, all of the old rules went out the window.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think Fire Drake from the revised Get of Fenris book would make a decent Totem for a member of House Verditus, and Xaos/Thig could probably find common ground with Cockroach, Donna Matrix, and other Tech Totems. It should just be somewhat less common for Hermetics, who already start out on the right foot with Hermes from the Infinite Tapestry, and the fact that for many of the Hermetics, Totems and the humility that goes with them isn't really their schtick. Then again, they DO desire to be like Hermes the Thrice Great, who is described in Rev OoH as being &quot;the greatest of kings, the greatest of philosophers, and the greatest of priests.&quot; Undoubtedly, some in the Order will decide to go for it. And even though gods like Ra, Marduk, Hermes, Ishtar, Vulcan, and Odin will see more Hermetics looking to strike an alliance with them than the spirits that the Fera serve, money is always a draw and someone in charge of their Cabal's/Chantry's finances could easily seek out an alliance with whatever spirit embodies the concept of profit and wealth.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There's the point. I can't really seen an impediment on his plan to have a totem and choose the House Fortunae. But the problems persists: I don't see how to fit his paradigm into any tradition and how it will work.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The game takes place in a post-pandemic scenario with economic recession. In catastrophe situations people believe more in the supernatural and it is in this scenario that my 7 players appear as &quot;intermediate&quot; magicians (not a beginner character's table kind). All of them has urban-like paradigms: a Euthanatos police officer, a activist rebel hollow one, a verbenae nurse, an car mechanic Son of Ether. an drug addict cultist and this guy.- his paradigm was fully based on three books: spirit ways (who says about hermetics having totens), the tradition book of the Order of Hermes (he was fascinated with House Fortunae) and a &quot;real world&quot; chaos magick book named &quot;chaostopia&quot; (that talks about the nature of the money spirit and other things).</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The chronicle is about the New York city spirit dying (something like Chicago Spirit in the book of madness) and this capel is trying do save him and stop the technocracy actions over the &quot;sick city&quot;.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">He was the most committed to creating the character and because of that I do not want to forbiden his character... But it's very hard, for real - I asked him to change the tradition to Dreamspeaker.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408646#post1408646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Totems have costs. You limit your freedom and thus ritually gain power from it. If he wants a totem that;s not going to limit him. Coyote is right there and more than wiling to &quot;help&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">not about the limitation, but what limitation.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408651#post1408651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried writing a response to this earlier on my phone, but kept getting pull away by RL and then it got lost when my phone logged me out &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> I think how well the idea can work depends a fair bit on how one chooses to interpret the word &quot;shaman,&quot; but I think there are at least two ways to handle this character concept:<br /> <br /> When saying they want to be a &quot;shaman,&quot; your player might simply mean &quot;a Mage whose magic is centred around summoning, interacting with, or binding spirits.&quot; If that is all, then a member of the Hermetic House Fortunae might actually work really well. As posts above have mentioned, the concept of &quot;capitalism&quot; is a bit abstract for the Middle Umbra. However, it seems rather appropriate for an entity of the High Umbra, and summoning Angels from the High Umbra has been a component of the Hermetic tradition for a long time now.<br /> <br /> The more specific connotation of the word &quot;shaman&quot; goes beyond just summoning and interacting with spirits, however. It also tends to include reverence for the larger system, not simply a desire to exploit it for your advantage, along with a role as a mediator between the community and the spirit-world. If that is the sort of thing you're looking for, an &quot;Urban Shaman&quot; Dreamspeaker inspired by the Glass Walker material cited above would likely be more appropriate. &quot;Pure&quot; capitalism is a bit at odds with the idea of a shamanistic character in this sense, but someone who played the role of &quot;mediator&quot; between people and &quot;the market&quot; might try to achieve &quot;balance&quot; through things like regulation, non-profit work, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is trying to be a shaman, using saxophone instead of drums and everything. The character entered in the Umbra and realized that everything works on the basis of energy exchange (and there are the accountant umbrodes), and, for him, money is the basis of these exchanges in the material world, then the most powerful spirits are those associated with wealth and money. His plans are to use the flow of wealth to help the capel with resources and influence and trying to revive the power of New York City Urban Spirit, fixing what largely represents the city in the material world.<br /> <br /> <br /> The totem thing just was decided - he chooses O' Mighty Dolla'. My great problem now is: how this kind of spirit (money or wealth spirit) should work? and if instead of helping, anger the spirit? the coincident effects seens to be a lot of vulgar when dealing with something like capitalism... And, what happen if a wealth spirit of someone fortune be harm ou killed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26367-wickedone","name":"WickedOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T09:28:31-07:00","id":1408733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408575-questions-about-something-like-money-shaman-paradigm?p=1408730#post1408730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait what those Coyote demand as a totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>It have no bans... Any limit is against it nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26367-wickedone","name":"WickedOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T11:37:28-07:00","id":1408755,"title":"","content":"Oh so why doesn\u2019t everyone take Coyote as their totem? Plus I think they\u2019re are a lot commerce Spirts. Here\u2019s a list of commence deities that could serve as a totem <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Commerce_gods\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Commerce_gods</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com